<task id="010" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>BFF by-regarding read endpoint (entity-set-agnostic, impersonation + 2-rule filter per FR-01)</title>
    <phase>W1 — BFF Reads (CC-3)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <deps>002</deps>
    <blocks>020,080</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a NEW read endpoint to `Sprk.Bff.Api` that is the sole data source for the record-level regarding-mode Timeline (Surface 1, all 11 entity-sets) and MUST enforce NFR-03 access parity (impersonation + 2-rule privacy/internal-only filter) on every read — no message content may bypass the BFF filter. BFF-touching: publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification required; access-filter no-leak correctness demands code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5. Modifies `.cs` in shared `Services/Communication/` (additive).</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-01, NFR-03</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add a single new read route to the EXISTING communication endpoint group and a single new method to the EXISTING read service:

    • **Route** — `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}` on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` (add to the existing `MapGroup("/api/communications")` — NO new endpoint group).
    • **Service method** — `ReadByRegardingAsync(entityType, id, ...)` on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs`.

    The endpoint returns **all threads + their messages** for a regarding record, in the **same DTO shape as the existing R1 thread-id-scoped read** (reuse the models in `CommunicationThreadReadModels.cs`). It is **entity-set-agnostic across all 11 regarding families** (matter, contact, … per `RegardingFieldMap.All`): resolve the regarding record → find its `sprk_communicationthread` rows by regarding → fetch the `sprk_communication` messages for those threads via an `or`-filter on thread id → run them through the SAME access filter the R1 read path uses.

    **NFR-03 access parity is the load-bearing correctness property.** The read MUST route through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` (the blessed impersonation read path) + `Access/CommunicationAccessFilter.cs` (the 2-rule privacy + internal-only filter). Do **NOT** author a new access mechanism, a bespoke ACL, or reintroduce **membership-union on reads** (retired 2026-07-16 — `../messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/access-model-decision.md`). Privacy + internal-only filtering is composed exactly as the existing thread-id read composes it; a private thread the caller has no grant for, and an internal-only message the caller may not see, MUST be absent from the result.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication subsystem. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` + `Services/Communication/` reads. Fluent in ADR-028 (the impersonation read path is the blessed mechanism — do not fork), ADR-008 (endpoint filters), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails), ADR-024 (11-entity regarding family / `RegardingFieldMap.All`), the R1 impersonation + 2-rule access model (`CommunicationAccessFilter`), NFR-03 access parity, `docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md`, §10 BFF Hygiene, and §11 Component Justification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}` endpoint exists on the existing communication group, backed by a new `ReadByRegardingAsync` on `CommunicationThreadReadService`, returning a regarding record's threads + messages in the R1 DTO shape, entity-set-agnostic across all 11 families. Every read routes through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `CommunicationAccessFilter` (impersonation + 2-rule) — no new access logic, no membership-union — so a caller sees ONLY authorized messages and private/internal-only content never leaks. The endpoint carries the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails and is registered unconditionally. Build clean; endpoint + access-filter tests pass (incl. ≥3 of the 11 entity-sets + negative private/internal-only cases); publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Surface 1 (the record-level regarding-mode Timeline PCF placed on all 11 regarding-family entity forms, task 020/021/022) renders a record's threads as collapsible groups → per-thread interleaved email+chat timelines. Its ONLY data source is this endpoint. Today the communication read surface is **thread-id-scoped only** (`CommunicationEndpoints.cs` exposes send / status / direct-thread; the R1 read path in `CommunicationThreadReadService` reads a single thread's messages). There is no way to list "all threads for a record" — task 010 adds it.

      Component Justification (§11): (1) **Existing** — grep-verified: `CommunicationEndpoints.cs` is thread-id-scoped; no route returns a regarding record's threads. But `CommunicationThreadReadService` + `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `CommunicationAccessFilter` already own the impersonation read + 2-rule filter, and `RegardingFieldMap` already owns the 11-entity map. (2) **Extension** — this is ONE additive route + ONE additive service method reusing all four existing pieces; it introduces **no new service, no new access mechanism, no second filter**. The route is new only because REST needs a new path; the logic is reuse. (3) **Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete)** — without `by-regarding` the regarding-mode Timeline (FR-03/04) has no data source and Surface 1 renders nothing (FR-01 acceptance fails); if the read bypassed the access filter, a private-thread or internal-only message would leak to an unauthorized caller (NFR-03 security failure). Named contract failures, not "future flexibility."

      NFR-03 access parity (binding): the new read surface MUST apply R1's impersonation + 2-rule (privacy + internal-only) filter and MUST NOT reintroduce membership-union on reads (retired 2026-07-16). The query is entity-set-agnostic: the regarding lookup varies by family (per `RegardingFieldMap`) but the message fetch (`or`-filter on thread id) and the access filter are identical across all 11 — server cost is flat regardless of entity type.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (ADD `by-regarding` route to the existing `/api/communications` group)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs (ADD `ReadByRegardingAsync`)</file>
