  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F/§G + §11 Component Justification + `docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` (confirms BFF read for the Timeline, not `Xrm.WebApi`) + `../messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/access-model-decision.md` (no membership-union) before adding the endpoint.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `CommunicationThreadReadService.cs`, `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.cs`, `CommunicationAccessFilter.cs`, `CommunicationThreadReadModels.cs`, and `RegardingFieldMap.cs` to identify the exact impersonation-query entry point + the access-filter call + the DTO shape to reuse, and the 11-entity regarding lookup names.</step>
    <step order="3">Grep the existing `CommunicationEndpoints.cs` + read service to confirm no `by-regarding` / regarding-scoped read route exists (§11 existing-question evidence).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement `ReadByRegardingAsync(entityType, id, ...)` on `CommunicationThreadReadService`: resolve the regarding thread rows via `RegardingFieldMap` (entity-set-agnostic) → fetch `sprk_communication` messages for those threads via an `or`-filter on thread id through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` → compose privacy + internal-only via `CommunicationAccessFilter` → project into the R1 DTO shape (`CommunicationThreadReadModels`). No new filter, no membership-union.</step>
    <step order="5">Add `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}` to the existing `/api/communications` group in `CommunicationEndpoints.cs`: bind `entityType` + `id`, call `ReadByRegardingAsync`, apply the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails (not-found / forbidden / bad `entityType`); register unconditionally (ADR-032/ADR-010).</step>
    <step order="6">Write tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`: (a) endpoint returns a regarding record's threads + messages in the R1 DTO shape; (b) coverage across **≥3 of the 11 entity-sets** (e.g. matter, contact, one more) confirming entity-set-agnostic behavior; (c) NEGATIVE — a caller WITHOUT a grant to a private thread receives NONE of its messages; (d) NEGATIVE — an internal-only message is absent for a caller who may not see it; (e) the read routes through the impersonation query + `CommunicationAccessFilter` and introduces NO second filter and NO membership-union (grep/diff-verifiable assertion).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing communication tests still pass (characterization green).</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0 (no new packages).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus access-filter no-leak / no second mechanism / no membership-union); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-01/NFR-03 filtering, ADR-028 impersonation-path reuse, ADR-008/019/024, §11 justification). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; shared `Services/Communication/`; coordinate with `spaarke-notification-spine-r1` + email-r4 merged state).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (010 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (regarding-resolution entry point, DTO reuse, access-filter reuse point, entity-sets covered by tests).</step>
  </steps>

