  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}` exists on the existing `/api/communications` group and returns a regarding record's threads + messages in the same DTO shape as the R1 thread-id read (reuses `CommunicationThreadReadModels`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ReadByRegardingAsync` on `CommunicationThreadReadService` resolves threads entity-set-agnostically via `RegardingFieldMap.All` and fetches messages via an `or`-filter on thread id.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The read routes through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `CommunicationAccessFilter` — no new access mechanism, no second/divergent filter, and NO membership-union is reintroduced (grep/diff-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests cover ≥3 of the 11 regarding entity-sets and confirm identical fetch + filter behavior across them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a caller without a grant to a private thread receives NONE of that thread's messages from `by-regarding`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an internal-only message is absent from `by-regarding` for a caller who may not see it (2-rule filter honored).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The route carries the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails (not-found / forbidden / bad entityType) and is registered unconditionally (ADR-032).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; existing communication tests still pass; publish-size delta ≈ 0 vs ~46.99 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 002 (thread typed-regarding lookups + Lookup discriminator — the regarding resolution this endpoint reads over). Blocks 020 (the regarding-mode Timeline component consumes this endpoint) and 080 (access-parity seam tests). The single most important correctness property is no-leak: the negative private-thread + internal-only cases are non-negotiable (NFR-03, security-sensitive). Reuse is the whole point — if reusing the R1 read path would force a change to `CommunicationAccessFilter` or `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`, coordinate; do NOT fork a parallel filter or reintroduce membership-union. `participant=` is NOT part of this endpoint (it is a filtered-query facet — task 011/051).
  </notes>

